<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		Invalidating an ancestor rebuilds the render-deferred div as a brand new widget that reuses
		the very same uuid. The timer of the widget it replaced is still pending, and the node it
		is going to look up now belongs to somebody else.
		1. Click "invalidate the parent" within 5 seconds.
		2. After 5 seconds nothing should happen: no JS error in the console (F12) and the deferred
		   div stays a placeholder, because its replacement asked for a much longer delay.
		3. The control below is left alone, so after 5 seconds it shows "control content".
	</label>

	<div id="outer">
		<div id="d" renderdefer="5000">
			<label id="inner" value="deferred content"/>
		</div>
	</div>
	<button id="go" label="invalidate the parent">
		<attribute name="onClick">
			<![CDATA[
				// the replacement waits practically forever, so anything that shows up within the
				// next few seconds can only come from the timer of the widget it replaced
				d.setRenderdefer(600000);
				outer.invalidate();
			]]>
		</attribute>
	</button>

	<label value="control (never invalidated):"/>
	<div id="ctrl" renderdefer="5000">
		<label id="innerCtrl" value="control content"/>
	</div>
</zk>
